From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 09:22:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(approval): resubmit lands on the -v2 form; stale
 Resubmit button is now cleared

Two defects surfaced while QC-ing the GBS SO/PO resubmit flow after the C4b
deploy. Neither was introduced by C4b.

1. Route split between the two resubmit entry points.
   /approval has always navigated to the unified -v2 forms (EC_SB_CFG maps
   gbs_so -> /gbs-so-form-v2, gbs_po -> /gbs-po-form-v2; the pre-deploy snapshot
   taken at 04:12 on 2026-08-03 already had them). But the modal path prefers
   the server's redirect_to over its own fallback, and Server Script
   resubmit_gbs_doc still returned "/gbs-so-form?edit=" / "/gbs-po-form?edit="
   -- the pre-unification forms. So the banner button and the modal landed on
   two different forms. Fixed on the site (Server Scripts are live-owned, not
   repo-managed): both branches now return the -v2 route. Recorded here because
   the GBS-side report attributed the non-v2 URL to this page.

   Note the old forms are not broken: all four form pages carry the same
   ec-gbs-form-edit-resubmit block, so ?edit= loads the doc and submits through
   resubmit_gbs_so/resubmit_gbs_po either way. What the plain forms lack is the
   ec-so-unified layer (mode bar, MODE='gbsrev', CSRF self-heal, MSO gate).

2. ensureButton() stopped polling once its button existed.
   The !shouldShow branch already removed a stale button and re-armed a 3s
   poll, but the shouldShow branch ended in a bare `return`. After the button
   was inserted the poll died, so when a resubmit flipped status to "Can sua"
   -- without a page reload -- nothing ever removed it, and it sat next to the
   banner's freshly rendered "Sua & Submit lai". That is the "2 nut resubmit"
   report. The branch now re-arms the poll, and the removal branch restores the
   Submit-on-GBS button it had hidden (previously left display:none forever, so
   a doc that came back to Approved had no way to push to GBS).

The blank-form symptom in the same report is a third, separate thing and is NOT
addressed here: the edit block alerts and bails whenever doc.status is not
exactly "Can sua", leaving the create form behind it visible. Any navigation to
?edit=<id> that has not first gone through resubmit_gbs_doc reproduces it.

main_section.html is re-imported verbatim from live, which had also picked up
two site-authored edits since C4b (ec-resubmit-realuser-v1,
ec-drift-settled-guard-v1) -- see page_sync.py for what each does. Net
repo -> live is +23/-1 lines, purely additive apart from the one replaced
`if (existing) return;`. BASELINE_SHA256 bumped and the C4b value moved into
SUPERSEDES_SHA256 in the same commit, per the drift-lock contract.

Verified on team.ecentric.vn: both writes are byte-identical round-trips; all
20 script blocks in the page pass `node --check` before and after; the patched
Server Script executes and bails safely on a doc that is not Approved+rejected.

